<https://archive.org/details/Fsi-ConversationalFinnish-StudentText>
    dcterms:title "Conversational Finnish / Suomea keskustellen (Foreign Service Institute, 1987), textbook as scanned on the Internet Archive (item \"FSI - Conversational Finnish - Student Text\")" ;
    dcterms:creator "Aili Rytkonen-Bell (as the scan's OCR text spells it) and H. David Argoff, with the FSI School of Language Studies Finnish teaching staff; Foreign Service Institute, U.S. Department of State" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "A work of the United States Government: the title page reads \"FOREIGN SERVICE INSTITUTE U.S. DEPARTMENT OF STATE\" and 1987, the introduction says \"Conversational Finnish is the work of the FSI School of Language Studies Finnish teaching staff\" and is signed \"Ambassador Raymond C Ewing, Dean, School of Language Studies, Foreign Service Institute, U.S. Department of State\", the last page carries the U.S. Government Printing Office imprint (\"U. S, GOVERNMENT PRINTING OfFICE ■ 1987\", as the OCR reads it), and the text carries no copyright notice. 17 U.S.C. § 105 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/105): \"Copyright protection under this title is not available for any work of the United States Government\". The Internet Archive item's metadata (https://archive.org/metadata/Fsi-ConversationalFinnish-StudentText) gives licenseurl \"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/publicdomain/\". Recorded here with the Public Domain Mark: free of known copyright."@en .

